## Algorithms
- [ ] Add measure distance command
- [ ] **A classifier with empty input classes brings "removed" objects back** (user report 2026-10-20): "Object classifier (remove small objects) -> AI object classifier" has the small objects in the results again; the other order works. A removed object only loses its classes and stays in `object_cache`; empty input classes select every visible object, class-less ones too (`matches_input` in `ai_object_classifier.rs`, the same filter in `classify_objects.rs`), and "Reclassify on match" / "Add class" gives them a class again. Same with a second Object classifier. Workaround: set the input classes. Fix (decide - changes the documented "regardless of its current class"): (A, preferred) empty input classes = all objects that still have a class, in both classifiers; or (B) drop objects from the cache when their last class goes. Check first whether a step or export uses class-less objects on purpose.
