  - [ ] An empty cell says why (e.g. "a channel doesn't vary").
  - [ ] Benchmark object measurements on a big analysis (the value is a correlated subquery per object - DuckDB decorrelates it, unmeasured).
  - [ ] Look at the picker's "Measurements" group in the real app.
- [x] Export (2026-10-22): measurement columns in the existing kinds (the dialog's column picker lists them; per image / plate / well the same values as the views; not in the image heatmap). New: "Measurements - one row per value" (`ResultExport::with_measurements`, `measurements.{csv,xlsx}`; the `measurements` table's columns, filtered by the chosen images, planes and measurement columns - none chosen: all; only offered when the analysis has measurements, `ResultsState.has-measurements`). Parquet also writes `measurements.parquet`. CLI: `export csv|xlsx --measurements`.
